From: kadaxo <105596590+kadaxo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Share key state across keyboard HID interfaces

Raw input tracked key state per device handle and the aggregator reported a
key as held if any keyboard had it down. Many keyboards expose more than one
keyboard interface (a boot interface plus an NKRO one) and, once several keys
are held, report a key's press on one interface and its release on the other.
The device that saw the press never saw the release, so the key stayed held
until it was pressed and released on that same interface again. Apply raw
keyboard events to every keyboard through the aggregator.

With the state shared, ysKeyboardAggregator::ProcessKeyTransition must consume
the transition on all keyboards; it used to short-circuit after the first one,
which would have made a single press register on consecutive frames.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/yds_keyboard_aggregator.cpp  | 3 ++-
 src/yds_windows_input_system.cpp | 5 ++++-
 2 files changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/yds_keyboard_aggregator.cpp b/src/yds_keyboard_aggregator.cpp
index ed66bbbf..bfe8bf41 100644
--- a/src/yds_keyboard_aggregator.cpp
+++ b/src/yds_keyboard_aggregator.cpp
@@ -30,7 +30,8 @@ bool ysKeyboardAggregator::ProcessKeyTransition(ysKey::Code key, ysKey::State st
 
     const int keyboardCount = GetKeyboardCount();
     for (int i = 0; i < keyboardCount; ++i) {
-        result = result || m_keyboards[i]->ProcessKeyTransition(key, state);
+        // Consume the transition on every keyboard, not just the first that has it
+        if (m_keyboards[i]->ProcessKeyTransition(key, state)) result = true;
     }
 
     return result;
diff --git a/src/yds_windows_input_system.cpp b/src/yds_windows_input_system.cpp
index da7e2a07..53e0a445 100644
--- a/src/yds_windows_input_system.cpp
+++ b/src/yds_windows_input_system.cpp
@@ -268,7 +268,10 @@ int ysWindowsInputSystem::ProcessInputMessage(HRAWINPUT lparam) {
             newState = ysKey::State::DownTransition; // Default
             if (raw->data.keyboard.Flags & RI_KEY_BREAK) newState = ysKey::State::UpTransition;
 
-            keyboard->SetKeyState(index, newState, newConf);
+            // A physical keyboard can expose several HID interfaces (e.g. a boot
+            // interface plus an NKRO one) and report a key's press on one and its
+            // release on another, so share key state across all keyboards
+            GetKeyboardAggregator()->SetKeyState(index, newState, newConf);
         }
         else if (raw->header.dwType == RIM_TYPEMOUSE) {
             ysMouse *mouse = device->GetAsMouse();
-- 
